==Restrictions==
*Fixed lineup: [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave Cat]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]], [[Undead Cat (Special Cat)|Bake-Nyanko]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]].

==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*4 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 8.67 seconds<sup>260f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You should have most, if not all of the [[Empire of Cats]] [[Treasure|Treasures]] by now, as without them the One Horn will be extremely difficult to get rid of.

This stage introduces the zombie trait: dangerous enemies that are capable of burrowing under your units and revive at a certain amount of health after being killed. However, units with the [[Zombie Killer]] (ZKiller for short) ability can prevent them from reviving.

The zombies here are at very low magnifications, however they are still very dangerous. You are provided with a surplus of anti-zombie units, keep spamming everything and you'll win eventually.

==Hints==
The first hint can be viewed within the Enemies Appearing window before beginning the stage. The second and third only appear as defeat messages when failing it.
*Purple Zombie enemies<br>can revive even after being defeated.<br>{{Color|Blue|Zombie Killer}} units can defeat<br>Zombies and keep them from reviving
*Be sure not to spend all of your Money<br>to stay prepared for burrowing Zombies.
*Don't underestimate the remains of<br>fallen Zombies... Save Money so you<br>can respond when they end up reviving!

